","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-17d.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":172},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"9bd39a75acbcb5478fff61d8840aa965466b836699326cde17008d22fec802a0","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-17d.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":8266},"state":{"digest":"a42d94d406e92e294f542bdb7ccadbc66d414dbbf8486ecb19cda88f436d478d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-17d.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-09-23T23:40:15.051791+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-17d.1","local_name":"sase-17d.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-17d","agent_clan_generation":"20260923191831","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-17d.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-17d[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Agents tab agent data decks and cards[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The Agents tab replaces its metadata panel and its Files and LLM [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Calls panels with one deck-panel type. It shows one or two panels, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]stacked top and bottom or side by side, and each panel shows an [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]agent data deck (Main, Files or Tools) made of agent data cards. A [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]deck renders all of its cards on one page when they fit a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]configurable threshold and one card per page otherwise. Keys cycle [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cards (Ctrl+J/K) and decks (Ctrl+N/P), split and unsplit panels (\\ [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and |), move focus (Ctrl+F), collapse the node panel (Ctrl+S) and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]zoom a deck in place (Z). The p view picker, the Z zoom modal and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the legacy panel modes are deleted, and glossary strands describe [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the new vocabulary.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]11[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agents_tab_decks_and_cards.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/agents_tab_decks_and_cards.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-17d[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-17d/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]LLM Calls stale-worker fix and split-key display[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]llm-calls-subject-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]llm-calls-subject-guard: stop LLM Calls worker results from painting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]onto a different agent, and teach key validation and display about [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]backslash and vertical_line so split keys can be overridden and shown.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Card-partitioned Main documents[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]main-card-partition[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]main-card-partition: every metadata builder wraps its output in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Context/Reply/Output/Summary card parts, error tracebacks move to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]top of the Reply card, and tree walkers learn the card wrapper. With the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flag off the panel renders as before, except the traceback fix.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Deck panel core behind the agent_decks beta flag[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-panel-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after llm-calls-subject-guard, main-card-partition[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-panel-core: create the agent_decks beta flag and the widgets/decks [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]package: DeckArea with two pre-composed DeckPanels, a hidden Main source[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]feeding MainDeckViews, per-panel Files and Tools views, tab-strip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]titles, empty-state cards, lazy loading and no-I/O availability probes. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Paged rendering only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Card and deck cycling keys[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-navigation-keys[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-panel-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-navigation-keys: Ctrl+J/K cycle cards and Ctrl+N/P cycle decks in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the focused panel, with sticky preferred cards. Ctrl+D/U, g/G and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bottom pin target the focused deck panel. Includes full keymap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]registration and the first flag-on PNG goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Split layouts, focus and split ratio[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-splits-focus[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-navigation-keys[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-splits-focus: \\ and | toggle top-bottom and left-right splits [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through a pure layout state machine. Ctrl+F moves logical focus and {/} [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resize the focused panel. Duplicate decks fan out to both panels, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no remounts on layout change.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retarget detail actions to the focused deck panel[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-action-retarget[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-splits-focus[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-action-retarget: inventory every consumer of the legacy panel ids [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and visibility helpers, then give each one a deck-mode path. Covers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]folds, hints, search, E, LLM detail levels, clipboard, footer, palette [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]context and auto-refresh, and makes the SLOW TOOL CALLS hint accurate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Node panel collapse and in-place zoom[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]node-panel-collapse-zoom[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-splits-focus[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]node-panel-collapse-zoom: Ctrl+S hides the node panel without unmounting[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]it and shows a slim node spine plus an info-row chip. With decks on, Z [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]becomes an in-place zoom of the focused deck panel that a second Z [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]restores.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Spread versus paged rendering[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-spread-mode[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-action-retarget[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-spread-mode: adds the ace.agent_decks.spread_max_screens config and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a pure decide_render_mode with hysteresis. Measures cheap lower bounds [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]first, renders Main and Files spread with titled separators and card [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]anchors, and keeps the reading position stable across transitions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Persist the deck layout across restarts[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-state-persistence[dim] · [dim][/dim]after node-panel-collapse-zoom[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-state-persistence: persist the layout, ratio, focus, node-panel [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]collapse and each panel's deck and preferred card to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]~/.sase/ace_agents_deck_state.json. Loading fails open and saves are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coalesced off the event loop.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cut over to decks and delete the legacy UI[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-spread-mode, deck-state-persistence[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-cutover: delete the flag's Off branch and the flag, the p picker, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the zoom modal, the panel enums and the legacy panel ids and CSS. Retire[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or rename the affected action ids, migrate or delete tests, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regenerate every affected PNG golden.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs, glossary strands and key-change notice[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-docs-glossary[dim] · [dim][/dim]after deck-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-docs-glossary: rewrite the Agents detail docs around decks and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cards, sweep stale zoom, picker and section-stop references, add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one-time post-update key notice, and add and edit the listed glossary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strands, then run sase memory init.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-17d","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-17d.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-10575dfca045e4940781da108c84a553","started_at":"2026-09-23T23:19:40.040267+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"comm